k. Land Navigation 36+20. Tracking: Humans and Monsters is Tracking (people) 25+15. Tracking: Animals is Track & Trap Animals 20+10. Wilderness Survival 30+10, Acrobatics 30+10, Prowl 25+15. W.P. Energy Rifle plus two W.P. of choice. The book prints no literacy and none was added. Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, for one other skill. The acrobatics bonus of the Felinoid race section (printed 109) belongs to the Mutant Jaguar entry and is not applied here. || RELATED: the book''s R.C.C. Related Skills, four plus one at levels 3, 7, 11 and 15. Communications +10; Domestic, Espionage, Pilot Related, Technical and Wilderness +5; Electrical, Physical, Rogue and W.P. any; Medical First Aid and Holistic Medicine only +5; Science Astronomy only +5; Pilot any except power armor and robots +10, which excludes Robots & Power Armor, Air Assault Armor and every Robot Combat row. Horsemanship is granted because the catalog files riding under its own category and Pilot is any. Mechanical and Military none. || SECONDARY: four plus two each at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, from the same list without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the custom cat warrior body armor (M.D.C. 60) is the flying-tiger-cat-warrior-body-armor row add-south-america-felinoid-gear.sql adds (distinct from the Hunter Cat''s heavy cat warrior armor, M.D.C. 90). The mess kit has no catalog row and is prose, as with the Sailor and Pirate. Energy weapon of choice is a choice among the South American RC-15/RC-10 lasers and the usual Rifts energy weapons. Four extra E-Clips. Archaic weapon of choice (usually a sword) is a choice among catalog melee weapons. Basic survival equipment is survival-kit. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits stored; the further 2D4x1000 credits in barter items are not coin and are prose."
