## Lore

Argentinean gene-engineers hunting for psychokinetic genes stumbled on a
strain of mutant cats that could levitate and even fly, slowly and low. They
spliced in genetic material from bats and produced a race that throws itself
through the air telekinetically and steers with grown gliding membranes. The
flying tigers also learned to wrap themselves in a telekinetic force field and
to hurl bolts of force. The Coming of the Rifts magnified all of it: they now
reach the speed of sound and out-fly most humans in jet packs or flying power
armor.

Most are mutant tigers (60%); the rest are mutant jaguars with the same
flying-squirrel membrane. They are the air force of Omagua. Every flying tiger
is trained for war and stands on call as militia; many serve in the army full
time and the others in Omagua''s equivalent of a National Guard. Their training
covers survival, tracking, navigation and languages, Spanish and Ancient
Egyptian among them.

## GM Notes

The flying tiger''s force field is its only mega-damage protection; the body
underneath is an S.D.C. body of 1D6x100 S.D.C. The in-flight combat bonuses
apply only while airborne. Starting kit includes 2D4x1000 credits'' worth of
barter goods on top of the cash.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'flying-tiger');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'flying-tiger';

